  "title": "The neural activity of auditory conscious perception: intracranial EEG epochs (Christison-Lagay et al. 2025; derivative: authors' 2-s grey-matter epochs)",
  "description": "This derivative dataset provides epoched, artifact-screened intracranial EEG from adults with drug-resistant epilepsy performing an auditory perceptual threshold task. A 75 ms target sound was embedded in white noise at each participant's 50% detection threshold, and trials are sorted into Perceived, Not Perceived and blank categories. The release contains 2-second grey-matter electrode epochs from 30 participants (32 recordings), repackaged from the authors' Dryad deposit into BIDS. Continuous recordings were not released. The position of the target sound within each 2-s epoch is not stated in the release, so epoch timing relative to the stimulus should be treated as unknown.",
  "methods_description": "Intracranial EEG was recorded from subdural grids, strips and depth electrodes at three clinical sites (Yale New Haven Hospital, Northwell Health, Mount Sinai). Participants reported whether they heard a sound and which one. Trials were sorted by behaviour. Epochs containing epileptic events were removed by visual inspection, and a four-stage artifact rejection was applied. Only grey-matter electrodes were retained, and removed channel-epochs are stored as NaN.",
